</div></section>

<section class="sec" id="enc"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="enc r">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Private by default</div>
      <h2>Your library is <span class="p">yours alone</span>.</h2>
      <p>bae encrypts everything on your device before it syncs, so your collection stays private, readable only by you. Not bae, not whoever stores the files, just your own devices.</p>
      <p>And you never have to think about it. It just works, quietly, in the background.</p>
      <a href="/architecture/encryption" style="display:inline-block;margin-top:8px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--fg-faint);font-weight:500;">Curious how the encryption works? It's all in the docs →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="flownode a"><span class="n"></span><span>Encrypted on your device</span><em>before it syncs</em></div>
      <div class="flownode b"><span class="n"></span><span>Private on your storage</span><em>only you</em></div>
      <div class="flownode c"><span class="n"></span><span>Only your devices hold the keys</span><em>always</em></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="center r" style="margin-bottom:34px;">
    <div class="eyebrow">Good to know</div>
    <h2 class="sech">A few things you'll care about.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="minigrid">
    <div class="mini r">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(134,224,200,.18);color:var(--mint)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17.8 19.2 16 11l3.5-3.5C21 6 21.5 4 21 3c-1-.5-3 0-4.5 1.5L13 8 4.8 6.2c-.5-.1-.9.1-1.1.5l-.3.5c-.2.5-.1 1 .3 1.3L9 12l-2 3H4l-1 1 3 2 2 3 1-1v-3l3-2 3.5 5.3c.3.4.8.5 1.3.3l.5-.2c.4-.3.6-.7.5-1.2z"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Plays offline</h4>
      <p>Your music lives right on your device, not just in the cloud. Lose signal or hop on a plane and it keeps playing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mini r d1">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(155,108,246,.18);color:var(--violet)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 10v3"/><path d="M6 6v11"/><path d="M10 3v18"/><path d="M14 8v7"/><path d="M18 5v13"/><path d="M22 10v3"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Original quality</h4>
      <p>No re-encoding, ever. Your files stay exactly as they are, and you listen at that same original quality.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mini r d2">
      <div class="mico" style="background:rgba(247,168,196,.2);color:var(--pink-deep)"><svg width="23" height="23" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 20h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2z"/></svg></div>
      <h4>Use what you have</h4>
      <p>Point bae at your sorted-just-so collection and it catalogs everything in place, no moving or copying. Backing it up to the cloud is opt-in.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" id="cloud"><div class="wrap provwrap">
  <div class="center r" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
